  "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{10}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{10}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}\\cdot {10}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}({10}^{2}-{10}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}(100-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
